The residual from the MIGRAD fit is small, however, so the observed discrepancy in the quadrupole amplitude must be compensated by other fit components. Perhaps the dipole, quadrupole, and/or 2D Gaussian were conspiring to fit the structures in the data. This discrepancy between the simplex and MIGRAD fit results appeared in the higher centrality fractions of cut bins

